# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# The line above is not enough on its own. core.autocrlf=true checks these files
# out with CRLF in the WORKING TREE, and anything that builds from the working
# tree rather than from a fresh clone — `podman build`, `docker build`, `make`
# under WSL — then sees carriage returns. career-mind lost an afternoon to
# exactly this: its container entrypoint died with
#   scripts/start_all.sh: line 4: set: - : invalid option
# while the deployed Space was fine, because Hugging Face builds from a clean
# checkout. A local build that fails in a way production never does is worse
# than no local build, because it teaches you to distrust the reproduction.
#
# Titan ships no .sh inside the image today (the Dockerfile CMD is inline), so
# the Dockerfile and Makefile entries are preventive, and *.sh is a guard for
# the first script anyone adds.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers stay CRLF, pinned so `* text=auto` cannot normalise
# them into something cmd.exe mis-parses.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Never let git rewrite bytes inside binaries.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
